PATCH 233: faithful reconstruction of the MGAVIDEO HUD-text glyph entry FUN_0000_1b5c -- resolve the
_DAT_1000_c736 host-pointer/width base-loss (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_mga_image.bin 0x1b5c-0x1b8f).

FRONTIER CORRECTION: the docs' "3068+5181" cascade anchor is STALE.  With the current patch series the
mission-start cascade (FIST_CASCADE) runs PAST the c6b4 3D-viewport render dispatch (which returns early --
geometry word[DGROUP:0x7ac0] is still 0, so mga:0x3068 is NOT yet reached) and crashes deeper, in the
6686 viewport STATUS-TEXT draw: 6686 -> 55ae -> [DGROUP:0x688] glyph vector -> mga:0x1b5c, at
`if (*_DAT_1000_c736 == -0x6000)` (RIP 0x811db84 = 1b5c+36).

ROOT CAUSE (watchpoint-proven on g_mem+0x1c736): the text-state pointer at DGROUP:0x736 is a 16-bit NEAR
OFFSET (asm `mov di,ds:0x736; cmp WORD PTR [di],0xa000`), but Ghidra typed `_DAT_1000_c736` as a 4-byte
`int**`.  Byte[2] of that 4-byte slot is 0x1c738 = the SEPARATE retrace re-entry counter DAT_1000_c738,
which the palette/vsync ISR FUN_0000_0b1f inc/decrements every frame -- so the composed "pointer" oscillated
0x00264c / 0x01264c / 0xff264c and *_DAT_1000_c736 dereferenced an unmapped address.  (This is the same
DGROUP:[0x736] base-loss class patch 131 fixed for the ABOUT-dialog twin FUN_0000_1d23/1d5f; 1b5c is the
HUD/viewport twin -- it blits via 1b98 + resets the clip box via 2e12 instead of 1d5f.)

FIX: read c736 as a uint16_t near-offset and rebase every access through g_mem+0x1c000, mirroring patch 131;
restore the 0x794/0x796 stores + the 2e12 tail that Ghidra dropped.  2e12 is a pure-DGROUP clip-box reset
(no base-loss).  Advances the cascade past 1b5c to the glyph plotter 1b98 (the next base-loss, same class).

Cascade-only (FIST_CASCADE, default OFF) => BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL for the 19 verify flows (the menu/dialog text
draws via 1d23, not 1b5c).  Sources pristine; fist_mga.c via build/.  Portable C.
--- a/fist_mga.c	2026-07-09 03:39:38.308456381 +0200
+++ b/fist_mga.c	2026-07-12 05:21:35.588478176 +0200
@@ -4345,11 +4345,25 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_1b5c(undefined1 param_1)
 
 {
-  if (*_DAT_1000_c736 == -0x6000) {
-                    /* WARNING: Subroutine does not return */
-    FUN_0000_2d6d(_DAT_1000_c736 + 0xe);
+  /* PATCH 233: HUD-text glyph entry (asm 0x1b5c-0x1b8f; DS=DGROUP=0x1c00).  Twin of 1d23 (patch 131).
+     The text-state pointer at DGROUP:0x736 is a 16-bit NEAR OFFSET, not a host int** -- Ghidra's 4-byte
+     typing spanned into the adjacent retrace counter DAT_1000_c738 (byte[2] of the "pointer", inc/dec'd
+     every frame by the 0b1f palette ISR) so *_DAT_1000_c736 dereferenced garbage (crash mga:1b5c+36 on
+     the 6686 viewport status-text draw).  Read c736 as a WORD offset + rebase through g_mem+0x1c000; if
+     the context's first word == 0xA000 (attached to the screen framebuffer) flush the pending scroll
+     (2d6d(off+0x1c)) and set rowtab word[0x794]=0x7c8 / pitch word[0x796]=0x140, then blit the glyph via
+     1b98 and finalize the clip box via 2e12 (both dropped by Ghidra). */
+  uint8_t *D = g_mem + 0x1c000;
+  uint16_t di = *(uint16_t *)(D + 0x736);                 /* mov di,ds:0x736 (near offset) */
+  if (*(uint16_t *)(D + (uint16_t)di) == 0xA000) {        /* cmp WORD [di],0xa000; jne 1b8b */
+    FUN_0000_2d6d((uint16_t)(di + 0x1c));                 /* lea bx,[di+0x1c]; call 2d6d */
+    *(uint16_t *)(D + 0x794) = 0x7c8;                     /* mov ds:0x794,0x7c8  (rowtab) */
+    *(uint16_t *)(D + 0x796) = 0x140;                     /* mov ds:0x796,0x140  (pitch=320) */
+    FUN_0000_1b98(param_1);                               /* call 1b98 (glyph blit) */
+    FUN_0000_2e12();                                      /* call 2e12 (clip-box reset) */
+    return;
   }
-  FUN_0000_1b98(param_1);
+  FUN_0000_1b98(param_1);                                 /* else: just blit the glyph */
   return;
 }
 
